  "body": "Refs #499 (Mac check of #458, LOT-085)\nClaim: mac/m2-lead\n\n**Problem.** The colour palette writes `[ff0000]x[/ff0000]`, which HFR leaves as literal text.\n\n**Cause.** `ReplyFormattingTarget.rawTag` returns the bare hex, as legacy does (`HFRswift/Swift/AnswerView.swift:35` on `origin/master`). HFR's tag is `[#rrggbb]` (capture `R41a`, HFR-PROTOCOL §6c).\n\n**Change.** `rawTag` adds the `#`. Only that case changes; the palette's `hex` values and the other tags stay. CHANGELOG-LEGACY row.\n\n**Tests.** `aColourTagStartsWithItsHash` expects `[#ff0000]x[/#ff0000]`; it fails on the bare hex.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Corrected color formatting in the reply composer. Text colors now use the `[#rrggbb]` format, allowing the selected color to be recognized instead of appearing as plain text.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
